Whisky Hab Privacy Policy
Last updated: November 11, 2026
Whisky Hab (package name com.gairigaun.whiskyhab) is an Android app that helps you start one habit or stop one habit. This policy explains what the app does with your information. It is written by [Your name or company] ("we", "us"). You can reach us at [your email address].
The short version
• We do not collect your personal information. We have no servers and no user accounts.
• Your habits, streaks and settings stay on your phone.
• Your photos are checked on your phone by an AI model. They are never uploaded and never saved.
• The app has no ads, no analytics and no tracking.
• The only time the app uses the internet is to download its AI model once.
Information the app stores on your phone
The app stores the following in its private storage on your device:
• The habits you create: the habit name, whether it is a "start" or "stop" habit, the check-in time, and whether it repeats every day or every 2 days.
• Your progress: your streak count and the date you last completed a check-in.
• Whether the AI model has finished downloading.
This information never leaves your device. We cannot see it. Habit names can be personal (for example, quitting smoking or junk food), so we keep them local on purpose. The app turns off Android's cloud backup, so this information is not copied to your Google account either.
Photos and the camera
When a check-in is due, the app asks you to take a photo with your camera so it can confirm the habit. The photo is held in your phone's memory and analyzed on the phone by the AI model. The photo is not saved to your gallery, not stored by the app, and not sent to us or anyone else. It is discarded as soon as the check finishes.
The AI model download
The first time you open the app, it asks to download an AI model (about 155 MB). The files come from Hugging Face (huggingface.co), which hosts the public CLIP model published by Xenova. When your phone downloads the files, Hugging Face receives standard internet request information, such as your IP address and device type. We do not send them anything else, and we do not receive that information. Hugging Face handles it under its own privacy policy: https://huggingface.co/privacy
After the download finishes, the app runs offline. The AI model runs on your phone using ONNX Runtime, a library that processes data locally.
